  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-24: "Continue with next tasks". Issue #3062 (read it in full with comments: gh issue view 3062 --comments; filed by mcp-r1 as their ISS-008, offered to this project) and DI-170 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md. Dev has three active contacts with the same full name; the Assign Task "Assign to" picker lists names only and the Confirm summary reads "Assign to: Name".

Entry points (search by name; origin/master e70ff38894): `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/LookupTypes.ts` (`ILookupItem`); `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/LookupField/LookupField.tsx` (the option renders `&lt;Text size={200}&gt;{item.name}&lt;/Text&gt;`, ~726); `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DecisionWizard/steps/ParameterFields.tsx` (`LookupParameter` → `ILookupItem` { id, name }; the draft label used by the Confirm summary); server `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/IDecisionLookupSearch.cs` (`DecisionLookupCandidate.Email`, already returned). Also check the Console's side-pane person lookup for the same field (task 193 moved Console lookups to the side pane): if it is the Dataverse "Lookup Records" pane, it already shows the email column; record what you find.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer: shared Fluent v9 React components (@spaarke/ui-components), DecisionWizard.</role>
  <goal>Each person option in the Decision wizard's inline picker shows the contact's email under the name, and the Confirm summary reads "Name (email)"; every other LookupField consumer looks exactly as before.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Extend, don't fork (FR-27/28): add an optional secondary line to `ILookupItem` (for example `secondaryText?: string`) rendered under the name only when present, so every existing consumer is unchanged. Keep the selected item's id and the value sent to the commit route unchanged; only shown text changes. A person with no email shows the name only (no empty parentheses). Load the fluent-v9-component skill before editing the component. LookupField is used by many projects: run /conflict-check, and keep keyboard/mouse selection and focus return (task 200) intact. Use display text only from the server's candidate; no new BFF field or route.</background>
  </context>
